1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Samuel Abravanel, was forcibly converted to Christianity during the Granada pogroms of 1391 and took the Spanish name '''"Juan Sanchez de Sevilla"'''.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Samuel fled Castile-León, Spain, in 1397 for Lisbon, Portugal, and reverted to Judaism - shedding his Converso facade after living among Christians for six years. Conversions outside Judaism, coerced or otherwise, had a strong imp
2 CONC act upon Samuel's grandson young Don Isaac Abravanel, later compelling him to forfeit his immense wealth in an attempt to redeem Iberian Jewry from coercion of the Alhambra Decree.
2 CONT ===========================================
2 CONT Also mentioned in Abarbanel Family Scroll – undated handwritten manuscript from the collection of the late Rabbi Shmuel Gorr, held by Chaim Freedman.
2 CONT
2 CONT Reference was made to “Elef Margaliot” 1993, Meir Wunder.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT During the persecution of 1391, but probably only for a short time, Samuel lived as a Christian.  He was a large hearted, generous man, who supported Jewish learning and its votaries.
