2 CONT Alomso became Virrey de Mexico after serving in Isla la Espanola.
2 CONT ES.41091.AGI/1.16403.15.2019//INDIFFERENTE,1952,L.2,F.234
2 CONT 1584 05-22 San Lorenzo
2 CONT Real cedula a los oficiales de la casa de la Contratacion para que dejan pasar al Nuevo Rieno de Granada a Alonso de Buendia, vecino de Torrejoncillo.
2 CONT
2 CONT Registry and Archive of Ejecutorias Caja 0309.0001 1516
2 CONT Patronato,284,N.1,R38 Autos de Pleito, 1557-04-08 Valladolid: Real Provision directed at the Viceroy of New Spain with inserts of the Autos: Catalina de Montejo wife of Alonso Maldonado, daughter of Francisco de Montejo one of the
2 CONC  first conquistadors of New Spain.
2 CONT Archive General of the Indias.Indifferente,Repartamiento de Indios. 1418,L.2,F.166:
2 CONT 1519 Was the Alcalde Mayor of Hispanola. Was given the Cacique Xinabueca and 30 Indigenous people by Diego Colon.
2 CONT Patronato,276,N.4,R.135 Appointed Oidor de Mexico 1530 04-05 Madrid
2 CONT Indifferente general,418,L.3,F.315 1512 06-19 Real cedula placed an embargo on Alonso's wealth.
2 CONT I am beginning to think seriously about the Maldonado of Isla de San Juan de Puerto Rico and how they just might be connected to this illustrious family. I have always had the suspicion that there were a lot more Maldonado living 
2 CONC in the Caribbean than previously thought. My discovery of many more variations within the Maldonado surname and the documented sources will hopefully have a lot of people looking around archives in Puerto Rico, Cuba and Santo Domi
2 CONC ngo to investigate these families better than they have been in the past.
2 CONT ES.51091.AGI/1.16419//PASAJEROS,L.4,E.3279
2 CONT 1564-03-22
2 CONT El Adelantado Alonso Maldonado, natural de Salamanca, hijo de Juan Alvarez Maldonado El Bueno, y de Dona Aldonza de Guzman, con Don Juan Maldonado, hijo suyo y de Dona Catalina de Montejo su mujer, a Nueva Espana donde tienes su m
2 CONC ujer y casa.
2 CONT Research Copyright 2008 John J. Browne Ayes
