2 CONT Felipe II von Habsburg, Rey de España1
2 CONT
2 CONT  b. 21 May 1527, d. 13 September 1598
2 CONT
2 CONT King Philip II of Spain
2 CONT
2 CONT  Felipe II von Habsburg, Rey de España was born on 21 May 1527 at Valladolid, Castile, Spain.
2 CONT
2 CONT  He was the son of Karl V von Habsburg, Holy Roman Emperor and Isabel de Aviz, Infanta de Portugal.
2 CONT
2 CONT  *He married, firstly, Maria de Aviz, Infanta de Portugal, daughter of João III de Aviz, Rei de Portugal and Katherina von Habsburg, on 12 November 1543 at Salamanca, Spain.
2 CONT
2 CONT  *He married, secondly, Mary I Tudor, Queen of England, daughter of Henry VIII Tudor, King of England and Catarina de Aragón, Infanta de Aragón, on 25 July 1554 at Winchester Cathedral, Winchester, Hampshire, England.
2 CONT
2 CONT * He married, thirdly, Elizabeth de Valois, Princesse de France, daughter of Henri II, Roi de France and Catherine de Medici, in 1559 at Palacio del Infantado, Guadalajara, Spain.
2 CONT
2 CONT * He married, fourthly, Anna Erzherzogin von Österreich, daughter of Maximilian II von Habsburg, Holy Roman Emperor and Maria von Habsburg, Infanta de España, on 12 November 1570 at Segovia, Spain.
2 CONT
2 CONT  He died on 13 September 1598 at age 71 at El Escorial Palace, Madrid, Spain.
2 CONT
2 CONT  He was buried at El Escorial Palace, Madrid, Spain.
2 CONT
2 CONT      Felipe II von Habsburg, Rey de España gained the title of Erzherzog von Österreich.
2 CONT
2 CONT  He succeeded to the title of Rey Felipe II de España on 16 January 1544.
2 CONT
2 CONT  He was invested as a Knight, Order of the Garter (K.G.) on 24 April 1554.
2 CONT
2 CONT  He was deposed as King of Spain in 1558. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He gained the title of Rei Felipe I de Portugal in 1580.
2 CONT
2 CONT      Philip, who was styled King of Naples and King of Jerusalem by his father, was given the title King of England. However, he hated everything about England - the climate, the food and the people.
2 CONT
2 CONT  A little over a year after the marriage to Mary, he left and returned to Spain. Mary saw him only once more, for a few weeks, in 1557.
2 CONT
2 CONT  In 1588 as King of Spain, he organised the Spanish Armada with two objectives in mind - to re-establish Roman Catholicism in his former wife's Kingdom and in Holland, and to protect Spanish trade with America. 
2 CONT
2 CONT On 28th July, a Spanish Armada (fleet) of 130 vessels sailed up the Channel. The English fleet had faster ships and guns with longer range and defeated the Spanish.
2 CONT
2 CONT Child of Felipe II von Habsburg, Rey de España and Maria de Aviz, Infanta de Portugal
2 CONT
2 CONT 1.Don Carlos von Habsburg, Principe das Asturias b. 1545, d. 1568
2 CONT
